 ## Overview
-The Sparse Voxel Brick Set is a sparse volume representation that groups Signed Distance Field (SDF) data into fixed-size cubic blocks called "bricks," each associated with a raytracing Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB) [S1, unofficial]. It balances memory efficiency and real-time constructibility, specifically optimizing for GPU cache coherency and parallel construction [S1, unofficial]. Unlike Sparse Voxel Octrees (SVOs) which vary resolution, or Grid Sphere Tracing which stores every voxel, the Brick Set uses a uniform brick granularity to balance memory usage and traversal speed, making it particularly effective in complex scenes [S1, unofficial].
+The Sparse Voxel Brick Set is a sparse volume representation that groups Signed Distance Field (SDF) data into fixed-size cubic blocks called "bricks," each associated with a raytracing Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB) [S1, unofficial]. It balances memory efficiency and real-time constructibility, specifically optimizing for GPU cache coherency and parallel construction [S1, unofficial]. Unlike Sparse Voxel Octrees (SVOs) which vary resolution, or Grid Sphere Tracing which stores every voxel, the Brick Set uses a uniform brick granularity to balance memory usage and traversal speed, making it particularly effective in complex scenes [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Octree-based structures](2792-octree-based-structures.md) by replacing hierarchical subdivision with fixed-granularity blocks for hardware-friendly memory access.
 
